USC: bypass the cache for modifiable memory on multicore parts

Each core of an SGX543MP has its own cache, so a load can see a stale copy
of memory another core stored to.  Always bypass the cache for memory that
the program may modify when there is more than one core.

diff --git a/tools/intern/usc2/inst_usc.c b/tools/intern/usc2/inst_usc.c
index 37dd546..a971428 100644
--- a/tools/intern/usc2/inst_usc.c
+++ b/tools/intern/usc2/inst_usc.c
@@ -15425,6 +15425,14 @@ IMG_BOOL BypassCacheForModifiableShaderMemory(PINTERMEDIATE_STATE psState)
 	{
 		return IMG_TRUE;
 	}
+	/*
+		Each core of a multicore part has its own cache, so a value another
+		core stored can only be seen by bypassing it.
+	*/
+	if (psState->uMPCoreCount > 1)
+	{
+		return IMG_TRUE;
+	}
 	return IMG_FALSE;
 }
 
